menu "tinyuz decoder"

    config TINYUZ_LITERAL_LINE
        bool "Decode literal-line control codes (tuz_isNeedLiteralLine)"
        default y
        help
            Literal lines store runs of incompressible bytes more compactly.
            The upstream tinyuz CLI emits them with its default compressor
            (`tinyuz -c`).

            Disabling this saves about 54 bytes of code, but the decoder can
            then only read streams encoded without literal lines
            (`tinyuz -ci`). A literal-line code in the input is then reported
            as an error.

            This changes the layout of tuz_TStream, so it is exported to every
            component that includes tuz_dec.h.

    config TINYUZ_MEM_SAFE_CHECK
        bool "Validate compressed input (_IS_RUN_MEM_SAFE_CHECK)"
        default y
        help
            Check dictionary positions, lengths and the input bound while
            decoding, so corrupt or malicious input returns an error instead
            of reading or writing out of bounds.

            Keep this enabled whenever the compressed data comes from a
            network, radio or any other untrusted source. Disabling it saves
            a little code and time and is only safe for trusted input.

endmenu
